---
const steps = [
	{ t: 'Add your files', d: 'Upload photos, video, audio, and documents from your browser.' },
	{ t: 'Let it organize', d: 'Alcoves sorts what you add and makes sense of what is inside it.' },
	{ t: 'Find anything', d: 'Search and browse your library by what it actually contains.' },
	{ t: 'Share it', d: 'Invite people to a library, or share a single item, on your terms.' },
	{ t: 'Use your tools', d: 'Connect assistants and scripts through the MCP server to build your own workflows.' },
];
---

<section class="section" id="how">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section-head center reveal">
			<p class="kicker">How it works</p>
			<h2 class="section-title">From your files to a library you can use</h2>
			<p class="section-lead">
				Add your files and Alcoves takes care of the rest, so your library is easy
				to explore and easy to share.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="steps">
			{
				steps.map((s, i) => (
					<div class="step reveal" style={`--d:${i * 90}ms`}>
						<div class="step-num">{i + 1}</div>
						<h3 class="step-title">{s.t}</h3>
						<p class="step-text">{s.d}</p>
					</div>
				))
			}
		</div>

		<p class="pipe-note reveal">
			The heavy lifting happens in the background, so the app stays responsive while
			your library fills in.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>
